<title>UK: British election diary - April 10.</title>
<headline>British election diary - April 10.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Election campaign events scheduled for Thursday include:</p>
<p>- Prime Minister John Major holds news conference at 0915 BST/0815 GMT, Conservative Central Office, with Education and Employment Secretary Gillian Shephard before leaving for campaign tour.</p>
<p>- Labour leader Tony Blair and economics spokesman Gordon Brown hold news conference at 0830 BST/0730 GMT, then Blair goes to Redditch and Warwick. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7768</p>
</text>
